    "phenomenon": "Stroke sensitivity at resubstitution Youden threshold collapsed to 8.42% (23/273)",
    "mechanism": "Tested: HistGradientBoostingClassifier overfits positive training cases on resubstitution, yielding training positive probabilities with mean 0.3478 and median 0.3490 (vs negative mean 0.0300). Maximizing Youden index (TPR - FPR) on this overfitted distribution selects threshold 0.1501. On unseen Cycle J test data, true generalization positive probabilities average only 0.0779 (median 0.0662), with only 23 of 273 positive patients (8.42%) exceeding 0.1501. When thresholds are derived using out-of-fold cross-validation on training data (preventing resubstitution overfitting), the 70% sensitivity threshold is 0.0424, which generalizes to 74.73% sensitivity, 68.77% specificity, 11.00% PPV, and NNS of 27.2 on Cycle J holdout.",
